course: dictionary
lesson: 10917
title: Volatile: a word with many faces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Volatile» has more than one meaning, so the words around it are your best clue. In science, a volatile liquid turns into a gas very easily, like nail-polish remover.
explain: Read the sentence and ask what it is about. «He's a good boy, but very light and volatile in character, and simply cannot hold his tongue.» The sentence is about a person, so volatile must mean his mood changes suddenly and he loses his temper easily.
explain: Money words can be volatile too. The text says, «volatile means changing very fast.» Swap that meaning into a sentence about crypto: a price that changes very fast is a risky price, so the meaning fits.
fact: Volatile is an adjective. It describes something that can change suddenly, quickly or unpredictably.
fact: A volatile liquid evaporates (turns into a gas) very easily, like petrol, so it must be kept closed and away from flames.
fact: A volatile situation can change suddenly and become dangerous or violent.
fact: A volatile person has sudden changes of mood and loses their temper easily.
fact: Volatile prices, for fuel, crypto or shares, go up and down quickly and unpredictably: £100 of crypto falling to £50 is a £50 loss.
exercise: In a science lesson, a volatile liquid is one that does what? | Freezes solid in the fridge | Gets heavier when left in the sun | *Turns into a gas very easily | Turns sweet when it is heated
exercise: The father says the boy is «volatile in character». What does this suggest? | Always calm and quiet | Very tall for his age | *Sudden changes of mood and losing his temper easily | Very good at running fast
exercise: What does «volatile prices» mean? | Prices that never change at all | Prices written in gold letters | Prices that are always the same | *Prices that go up and down quickly and unpredictably
test: A «volatile situation» in the news means a situation that can do what? | Turn into a cake | Stay calm and sleepy for years | Stop all the people from talking | *Suddenly become dangerous or violent
test: Why must a volatile liquid be kept closed and away from flames? | It makes a loud noise when opened | Its colour fades in the light | *Its gas can catch fire | It goes hard like rock
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to volatile in «volatile prices»? | Steady | Frozen | *Changing quickly and unpredictably | Cheap
